second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"In which significant event was HMS Birmingham involved?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"As the sun set over the bustling port of Portsmouth, the HMS Birmingham, a sleek Type 42 guided missile destroyer, docked at the naval base, its crew weary from a long deployment.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 267, \"text\": \"It was the summer of 1973, and the world was abuzz with the news of the Yom Kippur War.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 268, \"end\": 438, \"text\": \"The Birmingham's commanding officer, Captain James \\\"Hawk\\\" Hawkins, stood on the bridge, his eyes scanning the horizon as he reflected on the events of the past few weeks.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 439, \"end\": 579, \"text\": \"In the wardroom, the ship's executive officer, Commander Rachel Patel, poured over a stack of documents, her brow furrowed in concentration.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 580, \"end\": 697, \"text\": \"Among the papers was a confidential filing, marked \\\"Eyes Only\\\" and stamped with the crest of the Ministry of Defence.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 698, \"end\": 893, \"text\": \"The contents of the filing were cryptic, but Patel's trained eye picked out a few key phrases that made her heart race: \\\"Operation Nickel Grass,\\\" \\\"Israeli Defense Forces,\\\" and \\\"material support.\\\"\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 894, \"end\": 983, \"text\": \"As she delved deeper into the documents, Patel's mind began to piece together the puzzle.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 984, \"end\": 1157, \"text\": \"The Birmingham had been tasked with providing escort duties for a convoy of supply ships bound for Israel, a mission that had taken them into the heart of the Mediterranean.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1158, \"end\": 1202, \"text\": \"It was a routine operation, or so it seemed.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1203, \"end\": 1267, \"text\": \"But Patel's instincts told her that there was more to the story.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1268, \"end\": 1363, \"text\": \"She made her way to the captain's quarters, where Hawkins was enjoying a well-deserved whiskey.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1364, \"end\": 1444, \"text\": \"\\\"Sir, I think you should take a look at this,\\\" she said, handing him the filing.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1445, \"end\": 1554, \"text\": \"Hawkins' eyes narrowed as he scanned the pages, his expression growing more serious with each passing moment.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1555, \"end\": 1588, \"text\": \"\\\"What do you make of it, Rachel?\\\"\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1589, \"end\": 1622, \"text\": \"he asked, his voice low and even.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1623, \"end\": 1741, \"text\": \"\\\"I think we were involved in something bigger than we realized, sir,\\\" Patel replied, her voice barely above a whisper.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1742, \"end\": 1796, \"text\": \"\\\"Something that could have far-reaching implications.\\\"\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1797, \"end\": 1850, \"text\": \"Hawkins nodded, his eyes never leaving the documents.\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1851, \"end\": 1881, \"text\": \"\\\"I think you're right, Rachel.\"}, \"D1S20\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1882, \"end\": 1938, \"text\": \"And I think it's time we started asking some questions.\\\"\"}, \"D1S21\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1939, \"end\": 2094, \"text\": \"As the two officers pored over the filing, the shadows in the wardroom seemed to grow longer, as if the very walls were listening in on their conversation.\"}, \"D1S22\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2095, \"end\": 2253, \"text\": \"The HMS Birmingham may have been just another warship in the Royal Navy's fleet, but it was clear that it had played a significant role in a much larger game.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 66, \"text\": \"**HMS Birmingham Makes History with Grand Commissioning Ceremony**\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 68, \"end\": 273, \"text\": \"London, UK - December 3, 1976 - In a grand ceremony attended by dignitaries and naval officials, HMS Birmingham, a Type 42 guided missile destroyer, was officially commissioned into the Royal Navy's fleet.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 274, \"end\": 418, \"text\": \"This significant event marked a major milestone in the ship's history, solidifying its place as a formidable force in the British naval arsenal.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 419, \"end\": 633, \"text\": \"According to Rear Admiral John Fieldhouse, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Navy's Fleet, \\\"The commissioning of HMS Birmingham is a testament to the Royal Navy's commitment to maintaining a strong and capable fleet.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 634, \"end\": 756, \"text\": \"This ship represents the cutting-edge of naval technology and will play a vital role in defending our nation's interests.\\\"\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 757, \"end\": 850, \"text\": \"HMS Birmingham, built by Cammell Laird shipyard in Birkenhead, was launched on July 30, 1973.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 851, \"end\": 955, \"text\": \"After three years of rigorous testing and training, the ship was finally ready to join the active fleet.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 956, \"end\": 1134, \"text\": \"The commissioning ceremony, held at Portsmouth Naval Base, was attended by over 500 guests, including Lord Mayor of Birmingham, Councillor Harold Wood, and senior naval officers.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1135, \"end\": 1333, \"text\": \"Captain Michael Livesay, Commanding Officer of HMS Birmingham, expressed his pride in the ship's crew, saying, \\\"Today marks the culmination of years of hard work and dedication from the entire crew.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1334, \"end\": 1434, \"text\": \"We are honored to serve on this magnificent ship and look forward to the challenges that lie ahead.\\\"\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1435, \"end\": 1626, \"text\": \"The commissioning of HMS Birmingham brings the total number of Type 42 destroyers in the Royal Navy's fleet to six, further enhancing the Navy's capabilities in the North Atlantic and beyond.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1627, \"end\": 1811, \"text\": \"With its advanced Sea Dart missile system and state-of-the-art radar technology, HMS Birmingham is well-equipped to tackle a range of tasks, from air defense to anti-submarine warfare.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1812, \"end\": 1995, \"text\": \"Data from the Royal Navy's records shows that HMS Birmingham has undergone extensive sea trials, clocking over 10,000 miles and conducting numerous exercises with other naval vessels.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1996, \"end\": 2136, \"text\": \"The ship's crew has also undergone rigorous training, with over 75% of personnel holding advanced qualifications in their respective fields.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2137, \"end\": 2329, \"text\": \"In conclusion, the commissioning of HMS Birmingham is a significant event in the history of the Royal Navy, marking a major milestone in the ship's journey from construction to active service.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2330, \"end\": 2513, \"text\": \"With its advanced capabilities and highly trained crew, HMS Birmingham is poised to play a vital role in defending British interests and maintaining peace and stability in the region.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"HMS Birmingham\", \"scope\": \"event\", \"claim\": \"HMS Birmingham was involved in Operation Nickel Grass.\", \"answer\": \"Operation Nickel Grass\", \"quote\": \"The contents of the filing were cryptic, but Patel's trained eye picked out a few key phrases that made her heart race: \\\"Operation Nickel Grass,\\\" \\\"Israeli Defense Forces,\\\" and \\\"material support.\\\" As she delved deeper into the documents, Patel's mind began to piece together the puzzle. The Birmingham had been tasked with providing escort duties for a convoy of supply ships bound for Israel, a mission that had taken them into the heart of the Mediterranean.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Operation Nickel Grass\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Operation Nickel Grass\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Its commissioning into the Royal Navy\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"Grand Commissioning Ceremony\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}]}"
